  "evidence": "TEXT_G: Digital Bill of Rights, protect human rights law, oppose blanket surveillance; presumption against short prison terms with rehabilitation focus; end imprisonment for personal drug possession and allow medicinal cannabis; faster asylum decisions and allow work after 6 months; proportional voting and votes at 16; remain engaged in the EU and pursue deeper EU integration (Energy Union). TEXT_F: Retain cap on non‑EU workers, tighten short‑term student visas, two‑year wait for in‑work benefits for new EU arrivals, require English for public‑facing roles, more border staff and full exit checks; stronger terror controls with mandatory deradicalisation and updated powers; ban legal highs; protect the Human Rights Act/ECHR and advance LGBT and race‑equality rights; EU reform with no power transfers without an in/out referendum.",
